      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T16:00:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s an input regulation loop voltage (basically a 5V adapter would be allowed to drop to this voltage (e.g. 4.096V) before the current gets limited: we call this \"ramping\" in EC code).\n\nSo this is not safety-related (the voltage is already applied to the board before this kicks in, and changing this value won\u0027t protect the board in any way).",
